  "body": "All twelve common-root planning slots passed independent native replay. The longer horizon lowered average native branch cost by 7.33%, but was nonworse on only seven of twelve slots against a required eight. Correct dynamics improved common-pool ranking by 2.51%, below the fixed 3% margin. More short search offered no average benefit. All three contrasts failed their continuation rules; this tracking configuration is closed as evidence for learned adaptation.\n\n[Results, chart and limitations](https://github.com/kw2828/OpenJev/blob/main/research/reacher-common-root-diagnostic.md).\n\nThe protocol, source and paired inputs were published before execution at `c9a428ad9341db2aa74fe71f8fb6c3c8cc16f00f`. The archive includes all twelve raw slots, complete noisy native branches, candidate searches, cross-scoring, input arrays, source snapshots, native audits, reviews and the source episode records used to extract roots. Every archive member was reopened and hashed against `members.json`.\n\nExecution took 7.324 seconds and replay 13.034 seconds, covering 413,928 transitions each. This is an open-loop diagnostic on exposed engineering histories with ten distinct native states, not a closed-loop benchmark, learned model, deployment speedup or architectural result. No weights are included. Original path bindings and runtime assumptions are preserved.\n"
